loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\n        tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\n        parseable = call['parseable']\n        if tokens < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"prediction_tokens must be >= 1\")\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        # round to 8 decimal places\n        normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 8)\n        accepted_flag = bool(parseable) and normalized_gain_rounded >= threshold\n        if accepted_flag:\n            accepted.append(call_id)\n        diagnostics.append({\n            'accepted': accepted_flag,\n            'call_id': call_id,\n            'normalized_gain': normalized_gain_rounded\n        })\n    return {\n        'accepted_call_ids': accepted,\n        'diagnostics': diagnostics\n    }\n\nThat's it. Then escape.\n\nI'll produce the JSON response with the implementation string.\n\nNote: The output should be exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\". No markdown.\n\nLet me generate the escaped string. I'll do it manually ensuring proper escaping.\n\nThe source code as a string with newlines replaced by \\n, backslashes \\\\, quotes \\\".\n\nI'll write it out.\n\nBut careful: The JSON string must be valid. I'll use Python to generate and then copy. But I'm the AI, I need to output the final JSON. I'll construct it.\n\nI'll write:\n\n{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if 'threshold' not in case or 'calls' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case missing threshold or calls\\\")\\n    threshold = case['threshold']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"each call must be a dict\\\")\\n        required = ['call_id', 'los